.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt XTC_POOL 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_pool_create ,
.Nm xtc_pool_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_pool_add ,
.Nm xtc_pool_checkout ,
.Nm xtc_pool_checkin ,
.Nm xtc_pool_available ,
.Nm xtc_pool_capacity
.Nd bounded resource pool (checkout / return)
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxtc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc_pool.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pool_create "size_t capacity" "xtc_pool_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_pool_destroy "xtc_pool_t *p"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pool_add "xtc_pool_t *p" "void *resource"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pool_checkout "xtc_pool_t *p" "int64_t timeout_ns" "void **out"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_pool_checkin "xtc_pool_t *p" "void *resource"
.Ft size_t
.Fn xtc_pool_available "const xtc_pool_t *p"
.Ft size_t
.Fn xtc_pool_capacity "const xtc_pool_t *p"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A resource pool tracks a fixed set of caller-owned resources
(connections, buffers, handles) that fibers check out and return.  A
checkout blocks the calling fiber when all resources are busy, so the
pool doubles as a concurrency limiter.  This is the checkout / return
half of the connection-pool pattern; the supervisor's bounded dynamic
pool
.Pq Va xtc_sup_opts_t.max_children
is the spawn-workers half.
.Pp
The pool does not create or own the resources.
.Fn xtc_pool_create
sizes a pool for
.Fa capacity
resources.
.Fn xtc_pool_add
registers a resource (as free);
.Dv XTC_E_RESOURCE
is returned once
.Fa capacity
resources have been added.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pool_checkout
returns a free resource in
.Fa *out ,
blocking the calling fiber until one is free or
.Fa timeout_ns
elapses.
.Fa timeout_ns
of 0 tries once (returning
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
immediately if none is free); a negative value blocks indefinitely.
.Fn xtc_pool_checkin
returns a checked-out resource, waking one waiter.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pool_available
returns the number of resources currently free;
.Fn xtc_pool_capacity
returns the number added (free plus checked out).
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pool_destroy
releases the pool.  It does NOT free the resources -- the caller owns
them and must not destroy a pool with resources still checked out.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_pool_create ,
.Fn xtc_pool_add ,
and
.Fn xtc_pool_checkin
return
.Dv XTC_OK
or a negative
.Dv XTC_E_*
code.
.Fn xtc_pool_checkout
returns
.Dv XTC_OK ,
or
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
if no resource became free within
.Fa timeout_ns .
.Fn xtc_pool_available
and
.Fn xtc_pool_capacity
return counts.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_pool_destroy
returns no value.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xtc_pool_t *pool;
xtc_pool_create(8, &pool);              /* 8 connections */
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++)
    xtc_pool_add(pool, open_conn());

/* A worker fiber: */
void *conn;
if (xtc_pool_checkout(pool, 1000000000LL, &conn) == XTC_OK) {
    use_conn(conn);
    xtc_pool_checkin(pool, conn);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_sync 3 ,
.Xr xtc_supervisor 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
